From 3ceac7d369ea7f5fcb258fac49cb07e85401c960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 86/92] test: add fuzz targets for the P2MR rescue lane

- p2mr_rescue_token: the token and annex checks against their
  definition.
- p2mr_rescue_verify: voleith_verify_s1 through the C ABI, mostly with
  proofs of the right length, so that it gets past its length checks.
- p2mr_rescue: the interpreter's rescue path with a stand-in for the
  proof verification, as p2mr_slhdsa128s has one for SLH-DSA, against the
  rules written out: where a token is checked, R2 to R5 and R7, with and
  without SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE.
- p2mr_rescue_script_flags: script_flags with room for proofs, the real
  verifier and every prevout; test/util/p2mr_rescue_fuzz_seeds.py writes
  its seeds from the rescue vectors.
---
